CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Pick Charter A. The measurement likely holds as an L0 characterization if RE-A2 uses the tight assistant-text decode denominator and RE-A3 keeps CC+Codex as a hard gate; packet cites result-token mass at 63.3% CC / 86.1% Codex and session-clustered LB95 0.502 / 0.845. Gaps: only ~69 CC and ~89 Codex sessions, local/private live corpora, no production serving mix, no tokenizer/model sensitivity, and no dollar/GPU validation; publish as trace characterization, not universal serving economics.
RATIONALE: Charter A is systems insight/design because existing systems implement the knobs (APC/RadixAttention/KV reuse, prefill-decode disaggregation, offloaded KV layers) but do not answer where agent serving token mass comes from. Charter C is weaker for systems: shipping exact-prefix systems key reuse by prompt tokens/block hashes, so changed same-path file bytes should fail exact-prefix reuse rather than create a stale KV hit; its >91% changed rereads mostly measures low same-path byte reuse unless it defines a path-keyed cache mechanism. PROMPT_VERSION: v001
